From 3e2930a55a522a4e1f9767175fb106406722a431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saverio Moscardini <4923627+savemosca@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:49:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MP2K shadow: play at the canon direct-sound level

While the shadow substitutes, its mix replaces the Direct Sound FIFO
part of each output sample, through a fixed kShadowOutputScale of 24000
marked as a knob still to tune. The canon path scales FIFO bytes by the
DMA volume (x4 at 100%) and averages the enabled sides, times 48: a
full-scale DAC on both FIFOs gives 24576. The shadow's full scale (0.25
in bus float) gave 0.25 * 24000 = 6000, about 12 dB lower.

The PSG channels stay in the canon mix at their normal level, so the
balance between music and PSG shifted. Measured in MOTHER 3's overworld
music on an RG556 (90 s, shadow live 97.8%):
- music 12.6 dB quieter;
- music over PSG 3.4 dB instead of 15.9 dB;
- the player heard the PSG squares and noise as crackle.
The shadow's own stream was clean, with no jumps and no clipping.

The shadow's right/left now go through the same routing and scaling as
the FIFO A/B bytes: SOUNDCNT_H volume and L/R enables, averaged, x48.
The verifier is unchanged; it already compares levels in its own
domain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gba/gba_audio.cpp | 24 +++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gba/gba_audio.cpp b/src/gba/gba_audio.cpp
index c06eb9f..c247ea4 100644
--- a/src/gba/gba_audio.cpp
+++ b/src/gba/gba_audio.cpp
@@ -1032,13 +1032,23 @@ void GbaAudio::run_sample_event() {
         ChannelTap tap;
         int16_t s = mix_one_sample(slot, /*include_direct=*/!substitute, &tap);
         if (substitute) {
-            // Shadow output is the bus float domain (full-scale FIFO DAC =
-            // 0.25). kShadowOutputScale maps it to our int16 direct-sound
-            // magnitude — the loudness-match knob to tune in the audio
-            // oracle validation pass.
-            constexpr float kShadowOutputScale = 24000.0f;
-            int32_t shadow_mix =
-                static_cast<int32_t>(((sl + sr) * 0.5f) * kShadowOutputScale);
+            // The shadow's right/left are MP2K's FIFO A/B streams in the bus
+            // float domain (full-scale DAC = 0.25, i.e. 128 in s8 units).
+            // Route and scale them exactly as mix_one_sample does the FIFO
+            // bytes (SOUNDCNT_H volume and L/R enables), so the music keeps
+            // its level against the PSG channels. The former fixed 24000
+            // scale played it about 12 dB low (a full-scale DAC gave 6000
+            // against the canon's 24576).
+            const float fifo_a = sr * 512.0f;
+            const float fifo_b = sl * 512.0f;
+            const float a = fifo_a * (direct_a_full_volume_ ? 4.0f : 2.0f);
+            const float b = fifo_b * (direct_b_full_volume_ ? 4.0f : 2.0f);
+            const float direct_left =
+                (direct_a_left_ ? a : 0.0f) + (direct_b_left_ ? b : 0.0f);
+            const float direct_right =
+                (direct_a_right_ ? a : 0.0f) + (direct_b_right_ ? b : 0.0f);
+            int32_t shadow_mix = static_cast<int32_t>(
+                (direct_left + direct_right) * 0.5f * 48.0f);
             int32_t o = static_cast<int32_t>(s) + shadow_mix;
             if (o > 32767) o = 32767;
             if (o < -32767) o = -32767;
